        "math:completing-square-expression"
      ],
      "explanation": "Completing the square makes the least possible value visible. Since \\((x+1)^2=x^2+2x+1\\), rewrite the function as\n\\[\ny=2\\bigl((x+1)^2-1\\bigr)+3\n=2(x+1)^2+1.\n\\]\nFor every real \\(x\\), the square \\((x+1)^2\\) is nonnegative, so \\(y\\ge1\\). Equality holds exactly when \\(x+1=0\\), or \\(x=-1\\).\n\nThus the graph has its lowest point at \\((-1,1)\\), choice \\(\\mathrm{C}\\).",
      "id": "complete-the-square",
